  "oral_argument": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0bf000520325677686b868e688dfc4ce2c8491957f18f46626522729608f9ed2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0bf000520325-0000-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Souter asked whether the Government takes the position that a valid warrant need not contain an indication of the time within which it may be served or executed."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0bf000520325677686b868e688dfc4ce2c8491957f18f46626522729608f9ed2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0bf000520325-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Kennedy asked what would prevent the issuance of a blanket warrant, noting that there was a warrant for the premises to be searched."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0bf000520325677686b868e688dfc4ce2c8491957f18f46626522729608f9ed2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0bf000520325-0000-0005"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 6,
              "start": 6
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, chief Justice Roberts clarified that executing a warrant before the triggering event would be invalid because there would be no probable cause."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0bf000520325677686b868e688dfc4ce2c8491957f18f46626522729608f9ed2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0bf000520325-0000-0009"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 10,
              "start": 10
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Souter, justice Souter raised the issue of an ongoing obligation of reasonableness for officers executing a warrant without a time condition."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0bf000520325677686b868e688dfc4ce2c8491957f18f46626522729608f9ed2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0bf000520325-0000-0011"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 17,
              "start": 17
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Stevens asked whether a wiretap warrant must specify the telephone number and the time at which the officer may listen, or also the content of the conversation."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0bf000520325677686b868e688dfc4ce2c8491957f18f46626522729608f9ed2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0bf000520325-0000-0012"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 18,
              "start": 18
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked whether the Government would defend an anticipatory warrant in these circumstances, noting the postal inspectors knew the unlawful video would be mailed to one of 17 individuals."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0bf000520325677686b868e688dfc4ce2c8491957f18f46626522729608f9ed2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0bf000520325-0002-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 36,
              "start": 36
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, justice Scalia questioned whether a warrant that explicitly states it may not be served until a future time (e.g., 6:30) would be invalid."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0bf000520325677686b868e688dfc4ce2c8491957f18f46626522729608f9ed2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0bf000520325-0002-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 37,
              "start": 37
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg asked where the Fourth Amendment mentions time as a particularity requirement."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0bf000520325677686b868e688dfc4ce2c8491957f18f46626522729608f9ed2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0bf000520325-0002-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 41,
              "start": 41
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Breyer asked for clarification on whether anticipatory warrants are ever valid."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0bf000520325677686b868e688dfc4ce2c8491957f18f46626522729608f9ed2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0bf000520325-0002-0009"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 53,
              "start": 53
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Ginsburg, justice Ginsburg raised the possibility that exigent circumstances could justify a warrant execution after a known delivery of contraband."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Oral Argument",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0bf000520325677686b868e688dfc4ce2c8491957f18f46626522729608f9ed2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0bf000520325-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The United States obtained a warrant that specifically described the place to be searched and the items to be seized, based on an affidavit that a videotape containing child pornography would be delivered to the respondent\u2019s house and that the warrant would not be executed until after delivery."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Souter",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "0bf000520325677686b868e688dfc4ce2c8491957f18f46626522729608f9ed2",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-0bf000520325-0000-0003",
              "ev-0bf000520325-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "The central legal question was whether a valid anticipatory warrant must contain an indication of the time within which it may be served or executed."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Dreeben",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0bf000520325677686b868e688dfc4ce2c8491957f18f46626522729608f9ed2",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0bf000520325-0001-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 22,
                "start": 22
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Dreeben, there was ample probable cause that the respondent had attempted to receive child pornography through the mail before the triggering event, and the government could have obtained a conventional warrant at that time."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Reichel",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0bf000520325677686b868e688dfc4ce2c8491957f18f46626522729608f9ed2",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0bf000520325-0001-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 30,
                "start": 30
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Reichel, the magistrate determined there was probable cause to believe that, at the time of the search, the contraband would be present in the specifically described location."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Reichel",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0bf000520325677686b868e688dfc4ce2c8491957f18f46626522729608f9ed2",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0bf000520325-0002-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 37,
                "start": 37
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Reichel, under the Fourth Amendment, a warrant must clearly state the time limit on the officer\u2019s power to search in order to satisfy the Particularity Clause."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Reichel",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0bf000520325677686b868e688dfc4ce2c8491957f18f46626522729608f9ed2",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0bf000520325-0002-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 37,
                "start": 37
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Reichel, if the warrant is valid under the Fourth Amendment, the time of execution must be clearly stated on the warrant to satisfy the Particularity Clause."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "0bf000520325677686b868e688dfc4ce2c8491957f18f46626522729608f9ed2",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-0bf000520325-0003-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 59,
                "start": 59
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "The petitioner asks the Court to hold that the triggering condition in an anticipatory warrant is not subsumed in the Particularity Clause and therefore need not appear on the face of the warrant."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "United States (Petitioner)",
